 "formula_authority": "docs/engineering/rebuild/OBJECTS.md §Calibration and standards/CALIBRATION_WALKTHROUGH.md: x=(raw-b-beta*(D-b))/f, f=flat/flat_normalization, beta=exposure_seconds/dark_exposure_seconds",
 "formula_beta": "beta = exposure_seconds/dark_exposure_seconds = 600/600 = 1",
 "formula_note": "dark_contains_bias=true, so the dark's own bias pedestal is removed before scaling with beta: x=(raw-b-beta*(D-b))/f. With beta=1 the bias cancels algebraically and x=(raw-D)/f. Do NOT use the literal form (raw-b-beta*D)/flat when dark_contains_bias=true: that would subtract the bias twice (raw-D-b). The production authority is docs/engineering/rebuild/OBJECTS.md and CALIBRATION_WALKTHROUGH.md, not the shorthand formula.",
